<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8079" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cĭnyras</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cĭnyra</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Plin. 7, 56, 57,
			§ 195</span></i>), ae, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κινύρας</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A king in Assyria</i>, <i>afterwards
				in Cyprus; father of Myrrha</i>, <i>and</i>, <i>by her</i>, <i>of Adonis</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
				10, 299 sq.</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab.
				58</span></i>; <i><span class="en">242</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">270</span></i>;
			acc. Gr. Cinyran, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 6,
			98</span></i>; voc. Cinyrā, <i><span class="en">id. ib. 10,
				380</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cĭnyrēĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>Cinyrean</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">virgo,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Myrrha</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 10, 369</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Col. 10, 172</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">juvenis,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Adonis</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 10, 712</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">so also heros,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 10, 730</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cĭnyraeus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>of Cinyras</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">litora Cypri,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					8, 716</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cĭny-rēus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., the same: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">germina, i. e. Myrrha,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat. S. 5, 1, 214</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A leader of the Ligurians</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A.
				10, 186</span></i>.</div>
